.TH NMT 1 "2026-09-10" "nmt 0.3.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nmt \- terminal UI for managing Wi-Fi with NetworkManager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nmt
.RI [ flags ]
.br
.B nmt status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B nmt list
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-rescan ]
.RB [ \-\-interface
.IR name ]
.br
.B nmt speedtest
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-quick ]
.RB [ \-\-server
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-duration
.IR d ]
.RB [ \-\-streams
.IR n ]
.br
.B nmt version
.br
.B nmt help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nmt
is a terminal user interface for managing Wi-Fi connections through
NetworkManager. It lists nearby networks, connects to them (reusing saved
profiles), forgets profiles, toggles the radio, runs a speed test and manages
saved networks.
.PP
Without arguments it runs the interactive TUI. The
.BR status ,
.B list
and
.B speedtest
subcommands run headlessly and support
.B \-\-json
output for scripting.
.SH OPTIONS
TUI flags:
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interface " " \fIname\fR
Wi-Fi interface to manage (for example
.IR wlan0 ).
The interface can also be switched at runtime in the TUI.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
(status, list, speedtest) Print machine-readable JSON instead of text.
.TP
.B \-\-rescan
(list) Force a network scan before listing.
.TP
.B \-\-quick
(speedtest) Run the short variant: 5s download + 5s upload with 2 streams.
.TP
.BR \-\-server " " \fIurl\fR
(speedtest) Base URL of the speed test server. The default is
.IR https://speed.cloudflare.com .
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fId\fR
(speedtest) Duration of each phase, for example
.IR 5s .
.TP
.BR \-\-streams " " \fIn\fR
(speedtest) Number of parallel streams.
.SH TUI KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B up/k, down/j
Navigate networks.
.TP
.B enter
Connect to the selected network.
.TP
.B r
Rescan.
.TP
.B t
Toggle the Wi-Fi radio.
.TP
.B d
Disconnect the current network.
.TP
.B f
Forget the selected network's saved profile.
.TP
.B i
Show network details (BSSID, channel, frequency, rate, mode, security).
.TP
.B o
Cycle the sort order: signal, name, channel, security.
.TP
.B F
Open the saved networks view (connect, autoconnect, password, forget).
.TP
.B h
Connect to a hidden network by SSID.
.TP
.B D
Switch the managed Wi-Fi device when there are several.
.TP
.B /
Filter the network list.
.TP
.B s
Run a speed test against the active connection.
.TP
.B S
Run a quick speed test.
.TP
.B ctrl+r
Show or hide the password at the password prompt.
.TP
.B esc
Clear the filter, dismiss a message, or cancel a pending action.
.TP
.BR q " / " ctrl+c
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nmt/config
(usually
.IR ~/.config/nmt/config ).
The format is
.IR "key = value" ;
.B #
starts a comment. Supported keys:
.IR interface ,
.IR poll_interval ,
.IR sort " (signal, name, channel, security),"
.IR speedtest_server ,
.IR speedtest_duration ,
.IR speedtest_streams " and"
.IR speedtest_quick .
Unknown keys and invalid values are ignored with a warning.
.PP
Precedence: command-line flags, then environment variables, then the config
file, then built-in defaults.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NMT_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file.
.TP
.B NMT_INTERFACE
Default Wi-Fi interface.
.TP
.B NMT_POLL_INTERVAL
Status polling interval (for example
.IR 5s ).
.TP
.B NMT_SPEEDTEST_SERVER
Default speed test server URL.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nmt/config
User configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B nmt
exits with 0 on success, 1 on runtime errors and 2 on usage errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR NetworkManager (8)
